import K3Twists.CategoryTheory.Abelian.SerreClass.ExtensionClosure
import K3Twists.CategoryTheory.Abelian.TorsionTheory.Radical
import K3Twists.LinearAlgebra.Lattice.Mukai.AffineWeyl.Certificate
import Mathlib.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.Ext.Linear
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Lemmas

/-!
# Cartan descent: a torsion pair from an integer certificate

Let `𝒜` be a `k`-linear abelian category with objects `Q i j` (`i : ι`, `j : ℤ`) and integers
`κ i`. Let `F` be the extension closure of the objects `Q i j` with `j ≤ κ i`
(`CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionFreeClass`) and `⊥F` the objects with no nonzero morphism to
`F`. **Cartan descent** (`CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionTheory`): suppose that every nonzero
morphism to `Q i (κ i)` has image some `Q i j` with `j ≤ κ i`, that every such `Q i j` embeds in
`Q i (κ i)`, and that an integer matrix `A` bounds a truncated Euler form from below,

  `A i b ≤ hom(Q i j, Q b (κ b + 1)) - ext¹(Q i j, Q b (κ b + 1))`   for `j ≤ κ i`.

Then an integer vector `p ≥ 0` with `Ap ≥ 1` componentwise, an *integer certificate*, makes
`(⊥F, F)` a torsion pair, as Mathlib's `Abelian.TorsionTheory`.

## The proof

Put `L(Y) = Σ_b p_b · hom(Y, Q b (κ b + 1))` (`CartanDescentHypotheses.potential`). A nonzero
`f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)` is an epimorphism onto its image `Q i j`, and the long exact `Hom`–`Ext`
sequence of `0 → ker f → Y → Q i j → 0` gives, for every object `B`,

  `hom(Y, B) - hom(ker f, B) ≥ hom(Q i j, B) - ext¹(Q i j, B)`

(`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.ShortExact.finrank_hom_sub_finrank_ext_le`, from Mathlib's
contravariant `Ext` sequence and the `k`-linear structure on `Ext`). Weighted by `p`, these
bounds add up to `L(Y) - L(ker f) ≥ (Ap)ᵢ ≥ 1`
(`CartanDescentHypotheses.mulVec_le_potential_sub`). An object with no nonzero morphism to any
`Q i (κ i)` has none to the `Q i j`, which embed in `Q i (κ i)`, and so none to their extension
closure `F`. So kernels of nonzero morphisms to the `Q i (κ i)` can be taken at most `L(Y)`
times in a row, and `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.torsionTheory_of_potential` gives the
torsion pair.

A symmetric integer Z-matrix has an integer certificate if and only if it is positive definite
(`Matrix.IsZMatrix.posDef_iff_int_certificate`), so the torsion pair holds whenever `A` is a
positive definite symmetric Z-matrix (`CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionTheory_of_posDef`), in
particular for the Cartan matrix of an exceptional fibre
(`CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionTheory_of_fundamentalCycle`). Finite type is needed for this
argument: on an affine diagram a positive null vector forbids every certificate
(`Matrix.IsSymm.no_certificate_of_null`).

## The application and the fields

In the application `𝒜` is the first tilt of the coherent sheaves on a projective K3 surface `X`
at a big and nef divisor `H` whose null curves `C₁, …, C_l` (`H·Cᵢ = 0`) are smooth rational
`(-2)`-curves forming a finite ADE configuration, `Q i j = 𝒪_{Cᵢ}(j)`, and `A = (-Cᵢ·Cⱼ)` is the
Cartan matrix of the configuration. The fields of `CartanDescentHypotheses`, with their
sources:

* `finiteDimensional_hom`, `finiteDimensional_ext`: the `Hom` and `Ext¹` spaces involved are
  finite dimensional. `𝒜` is the heart of a bounded t-structure on `D^b(X)`, `Ext¹` in a heart is
  `Hom(-, -[1])` in `D^b(X)`, and the `Hom` spaces of `D^b(X)` are finite dimensional because
  `X` is smooth and projective.
* `exists_mono`: `𝒪_{Cᵢ}(j) ↪ 𝒪_{Cᵢ}(κᵢ)` for `j ≤ κᵢ`, from a nonzero section of
  `𝒪_{ℙ¹}(κᵢ - j)`. The cokernel is a torsion sheaf, so the sequence is short exact in the tilt.
* `exists_image_iso`, the epimorphism step: the image in `𝒜` of a nonzero morphism to
  `𝒪_{Cᵢ}(κᵢ)` is a sheaf `𝒪_{Cᵢ}(j)` with `j ≤ κᵢ`, and the kernel stays in the first tilt. It
  has no published proof and no human review.
* `cartan_le_hom_sub_ext`: Riemann–Roch on `X`, `χ(E, E') = -⟨v(E), v(E')⟩`, with Serre duality.
  At `b = i` the degree gap `κᵢ + 1 - j ≥ 1` on `Cᵢ ≅ ℙ¹` kills `ext²`, and `χ = 2` because the
  normal bundle of `Cᵢ` is `𝒪(-2)`: `hom - ext¹ = 2 = A i i`. At `b ≠ i` there is no nonzero
  morphism between sheaves on different curves and `ext² = 0`, so
  `hom - ext¹ = χ = -Cᵢ·C_b = A i b`; the transverse intersection points contribute to `ext¹`.

On coherent sheaves, in place of the first tilt, this torsion pair is a case of Yoshioka's
(arXiv:1003.2522, Proposition 2.1.1(2)): for the minimal resolution of a normal projective
surface with rational singularities and line bundles on the exceptional curves, the sheaves
generated by subsheaves of these line bundles and the sheaves with no nonzero morphism to them
form a torsion pair, written there with the torsion-free class first. For the contraction of
the null curves and the line bundles `𝒪_{Cᵢ}(κᵢ)` the two classes are `F` and `⊥F`.

## Which fields have no geometric instance

None of the fields has a geometric instance in the library: it has no coherent sheaves on a K3
surface and no tilts of them. The missing input is the bounded derived category of a K3
surface, a `2`-Calabi–Yau triangulated category, with its hearts, so the instance is a model:
`K3TwistsTest/CartanDescentModel.lean` meets every field in finite-dimensional vector spaces,
together with a certificate. The matrix side is checked on real objects: the Cartan matrix of
every exceptional fibre `Mukai.FundamentalCycle` has an integer certificate
(`Mukai.FundamentalCycle.exists_cartan_certificate`), and the fibre of the section of the
elliptic K3 surface has `A = (2)` with the certificate `p = 1`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.K3.EllipticWithSection.sectionFibre_cartan_mulVec_one`).

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.Abelian.CartanDescentHypotheses`: the inputs of Cartan descent.
* `CategoryTheory.Abelian.CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionFreeClass`: the extension closure `F`
  of the objects `Q i j` with `j ≤ κ i`.
* `CategoryTheory.Abelian.CartanDescentHypotheses.potential`: the potential `L` of a weight
  vector.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.ShortExact.finrank_hom_sub_finrank_ext_le`: the long exact
  `Hom`–`Ext` sequence in dimensions.
* `CategoryTheory.Abelian.CartanDescentHypotheses.mulVec_le_potential_sub`: the potential drops
  by at least `(Ap)ᵢ` on kernels of nonzero morphisms to `Q i (κ i)`.
* `CategoryTheory.Abelian.CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionTheory`: **Cartan descent**, the
  torsion pair `(⊥F, F)` from an integer certificate.
* `CategoryTheory.Abelian.CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionTheory_of_posDef`: the torsion pair
  when `A` is a positive definite symmetric Z-matrix.
* `CategoryTheory.Abelian.CartanDescentHypotheses.torsionTheory_of_fundamentalCycle`: the
  torsion pair when `A` is the Cartan matrix of an exceptional fibre.

## References

* K. Yoshioka, *Perverse coherent sheaves and Fourier–Mukai transforms on surfaces*,
  arXiv:1003.2522, Proposition 2.1.1(2).
* A. Berman and R. J. Plemmons, *Nonnegative Matrices in the Mathematical Sciences*, Chapter 6,
  Theorem 2.3 (the M-matrix criterion behind the integer certificate).
* V. G. Kac, *Infinite dimensional Lie algebras*, Chapter 4 (finite and affine type).
* S. E. Dickson, *A torsion theory for Abelian categories*, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 121 (1966).

## Tags

torsion pair, torsion theory, potential, integer certificate, Cartan matrix, M-matrix, tilt
-/

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Matrix Module

universe w v u

namespace CategoryTheory

variable {k : Type*} [Field k] {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Abelian C] [Linear k C]

/-! ### The long exact `Hom`–`Ext` sequence in dimensions -/

namespace ShortComplex.ShortExact

variable [HasExt.{w} C] {S : ShortComplex C}

/-- **The long exact `Hom`–`Ext` sequence in dimensions.** For a short exact sequence
`0 → X₁ → X₂ → X₃ → 0` and an object `B`, exactness of
`0 → Hom(X₃, B) → Hom(X₂, B) → Hom(X₁, B) → Ext¹(X₃, B)` gives
`hom(X₃, B) - ext¹(X₃, B) ≤ hom(X₂, B) - hom(X₁, B)`, when `Hom(X₂, B)`, `Hom(X₁, B)` and
`Ext¹(X₃, B)` are finite dimensional. -/
theorem finrank_hom_sub_finrank_ext_le (hS : S.ShortExact) (B : C)
    [FiniteDimensional k (S.X₂ ⟶ B)] [FiniteDimensional k (S.X₁ ⟶ B)]
    [FiniteDimensional k (Abelian.Ext.{w} S.X₃ B 1)] :
    (finrank k (S.X₃ ⟶ B) : ℤ) - finrank k (Abelian.Ext.{w} S.X₃ B 1) ≤
      (finrank k (S.X₂ ⟶ B) : ℤ) - finrank k (S.X₁ ⟶ B) := by
  have := hS.epi_g
  let a : (S.X₃ ⟶ B) →ₗ[k] (S.X₂ ⟶ B) := Linear.leftComp k B S.g
  let b : (S.X₂ ⟶ B) →ₗ[k] (S.X₁ ⟶ B) := Linear.leftComp k B S.f
  let c : (S.X₁ ⟶ B) →ₗ[k] Abelian.Ext.{w} S.X₃ B 1 :=
    Abelian.Ext.precompOfLinear hS.extClass k B (add_zero 1) ∘ₗ
      (Abelian.Ext.linearEquiv₀ (R := k)).symm.toLinearMap
  have ha : Function.Injective a := fun φ ψ h => (cancel_epi S.g).1 h
  have hab : LinearMap.ker b = LinearMap.range a := by
    ext ψ
    simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.mem_range]
    constructor
    · intro hψ
      obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := CokernelCofork.IsColimit.desc' hS.gIsCokernel ψ hψ
      exact ⟨φ, hφ⟩
    · rintro ⟨φ, rfl⟩
      simp [a, b]
  have hbc : LinearMap.range b = LinearMap.ker c := by
    ext χ
    simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.mem_range]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨ψ, rfl⟩
      simp only [b, c, LinearMap.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe,
        Abelian.Ext.linearEquiv₀_symm_apply, Linear.leftComp_apply,
        Abelian.Ext.bilinearCompOfLinear_apply_apply]
      rw [← Abelian.Ext.mk₀_comp_mk₀]
      exact hS.extClass_comp_assoc _
    · intro hχ
      simp only [c, LinearMap.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe,
        Abelian.Ext.linearEquiv₀_symm_apply,
        Abelian.Ext.bilinearCompOfLinear_apply_apply] at hχ
      obtain ⟨x₂, hx₂⟩ := Abelian.Ext.contravariant_sequence_exact₁ hS B _ (add_zero 1) hχ
      refine ⟨Abelian.Ext.homEquiv₀ x₂, (Abelian.Ext.mk₀_bijective _ _).1 ?_⟩
      simp only [b, Linear.leftComp_apply]
      rw [← hx₂, ← Abelian.Ext.mk₀_comp_mk₀, Abelian.Ext.mk₀_homEquiv₀_apply]
  have h1 := LinearMap.finrank_range_add_finrank_ker b
  have h2 := LinearMap.finrank_range_add_finrank_ker c
  have h3 := Submodule.finrank_le (LinearMap.range c)
  rw [hab, LinearMap.finrank_range_of_inj ha, hbc] at h1
  omega

end ShortComplex.ShortExact

/-! ### The inputs -/

namespace Abelian

variable [HasExt.{w} C] {ι : Type*}

variable (k) in
/-- **The inputs of Cartan descent** for objects `Q i j` (`i : ι`, `j : ℤ`) of a `k`-linear
abelian category, integers `κ i` and an integer matrix `A`.

In the application the category is the first tilt of the coherent sheaves on a projective K3
surface `X` at a big and nef divisor whose null curves `Cᵢ` form a finite ADE configuration of
smooth rational `(-2)`-curves, `Q i j = 𝒪_{Cᵢ}(j)` and `A = (-Cᵢ·Cⱼ)`. The library has no
coherent sheaves on a K3 surface and no tilts of them, so no field has a geometric instance
here; see the module docstring. -/
structure CartanDescentHypotheses (Q : ι → ℤ → C) (κ : ι → ℤ) (A : Matrix ι ι ℤ) : Prop where
  /-- `Hom(Y, Q b (κ b + 1))` is finite dimensional for every object `Y`. In the application the
  category is a heart of `D^b(X)`, whose `Hom` spaces are finite dimensional because `X` is
  smooth and projective. -/
  finiteDimensional_hom : ∀ (Y : C) (b : ι), FiniteDimensional k (Y ⟶ Q b (κ b + 1))
  /-- `Ext¹(Q i j, Q b (κ b + 1))` is finite dimensional for `j ≤ κ i`. In the application
  `Ext¹` in a heart of `D^b(X)` is `Hom(-, -[1])` in `D^b(X)`, finite dimensional because `X` is
  smooth and projective. -/
  finiteDimensional_ext : ∀ (i : ι) (j : ℤ) (b : ι), j ≤ κ i →
    FiniteDimensional k (Ext.{w} (Q i j) (Q b (κ b + 1)) 1)
  /-- **The embeddings** `Q i j ↪ Q i (κ i)` for `j ≤ κ i`. In the application a nonzero section
  of `𝒪_{ℙ¹}(κᵢ - j)` gives `0 → 𝒪_{Cᵢ}(j) → 𝒪_{Cᵢ}(κᵢ) → 𝒪_Z → 0` with `Z` finite; the three
  sheaves are torsion sheaves, so they lie in the first tilt and the sequence is short exact
  there. -/
  exists_mono : ∀ (i : ι) (j : ℤ), j ≤ κ i → ∃ m : Q i j ⟶ Q i (κ i), Mono m
  /-- **The epimorphism step.** The image of a nonzero morphism `f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)` is some
  `Q i j` with `j ≤ κ i`, so `f` is an epimorphism onto `Q i j` followed by a monomorphism. In the
  application: the image in the first tilt of a nonzero morphism to `𝒪_{Cᵢ}(κᵢ)` is a sheaf
  `𝒪_{Cᵢ}(j)` with `j ≤ κᵢ`, and the kernel of `Y → 𝒪_{Cᵢ}(j)` stays in the first tilt.
  This statement has no published proof and no human review. -/
  exists_image_iso : ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (i : ι) (f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)), f ≠ 0 →
    ∃ j ≤ κ i, Nonempty (Limits.image f ≅ Q i j)
  /-- **The numerical input**: `A i b ≤ hom(Q i j, Q b (κ b + 1)) - ext¹(Q i j, Q b (κ b + 1))`
  for `j ≤ κ i`. In the application, with `A = (-Cᵢ·Cⱼ)`, Riemann–Roch on `X`
  (`χ(E, E') = -⟨v(E), v(E')⟩`) and Serre duality give equality: at `b = i` the degree gap
  `κᵢ + 1 - j ≥ 1` on `Cᵢ ≅ ℙ¹` kills `ext²` and `χ = 2`, since the normal bundle of `Cᵢ` is
  `𝒪(-2)`; at `b ≠ i` there is no nonzero morphism, `ext² = 0`, and `χ = -Cᵢ·C_b`. -/
  cartan_le_hom_sub_ext : ∀ (i : ι) (j : ℤ) (b : ι), j ≤ κ i →
    A i b ≤ (finrank k (Q i j ⟶ Q b (κ b + 1)) : ℤ) - finrank k (Ext.{w} (Q i j) (Q b (κ b + 1)) 1)

namespace CartanDescentHypotheses

variable (Q : ι → ℤ → C) (κ : ι → ℤ)

/-- The objects `Q i j` with `j ≤ κ i`. -/
def generators : ObjectProperty C :=
  fun X => ∃ i j, j ≤ κ i ∧ Q i j = X

/-- The class `F`: the extension closure of the objects `Q i j` with `j ≤ κ i`, the
torsion-free class of Cartan descent. -/
abbrev torsionFreeClass : ObjectProperty C :=
  (generators Q κ).abelianExtensionClosure

variable (k) in
/-- **The potential** of a weight vector `p : ι → ℤ`: `L(Y) = Σ_b p_b · hom(Y, Q b (κ b + 1))`,
a negative weight counting as `0`. -/
noncomputable def potential [Fintype ι] (p : ι → ℤ) (Y : C) : ℕ :=
  ∑ b, (p b).toNat * finrank k (Y ⟶ Q b (κ b + 1))

variable {Q κ} {A : Matrix ι ι ℤ}

/-! ### The potential drops on kernels -/

/-- **The potential drops by at least `(Ap)ᵢ`.** For a weight vector `p ≥ 0` and a nonzero
`f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)`, `L(Y) - L(ker f) ≥ (Ap)ᵢ`. The long exact `Hom`–`Ext` sequence of
`0 → ker f → Y → Q i j → 0`, with `Q i j` the image of `f`, bounds the drop of
`hom(-, Q b (κ b + 1))` from below by `hom(Q i j, Q b (κ b + 1)) - ext¹(Q i j, Q b (κ b + 1))`,
hence by `A i b`. -/
theorem mulVec_le_potential_sub [Fintype ι] (H : CartanDescentHypotheses k Q κ A) {p : ι → ℤ}
    (hp : ∀ b, 0 ≤ p b) {Y : C} {i : ι} (f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)) (hf : f ≠ 0) :
    (A *ᵥ p) i ≤ (potential k Q κ p Y : ℤ) - potential k Q κ p (kernel f) := by
  obtain ⟨j, hj, ⟨e⟩⟩ := H.exists_image_iso i f hf
  have hfac : (Limits.factorThruImage f ≫ e.hom) ≫ e.inv ≫ Limits.image.ι f = f := by simp
  have hzero : kernel.ι f ≫ Limits.factorThruImage f ≫ e.hom = 0 := by
    rw [← cancel_mono (e.inv ≫ Limits.image.ι f)]
    simp
  let S := ShortComplex.mk (kernel.ι f) (Limits.factorThruImage f ≫ e.hom) hzero
  have hS : S.ShortExact :=
    { exact := S.exact_of_f_is_kernel (isKernelOfComp _ f (kernelIsKernel f) hzero hfac) }
  have key (b : ι) : A i b * p b ≤
      p b * ((finrank k (Y ⟶ Q b (κ b + 1)) : ℤ) - finrank k (kernel f ⟶ Q b (κ b + 1))) := by
    have := H.finiteDimensional_hom Y b
    have := H.finiteDimensional_hom (kernel f) b
    have := H.finiteDimensional_ext i j b hj
    rw [mul_comm]
    exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ((H.cartan_le_hom_sub_ext i j b hj).trans
      (hS.finrank_hom_sub_finrank_ext_le (k := k) (Q b (κ b + 1)))) (hp b)
  have hp' (b : ι) : ((p b).toNat : ℤ) = p b := Int.toNat_of_nonneg (hp b)
  calc (A *ᵥ p) i = ∑ b, A i b * p b := rfl
    _ ≤ ∑ b, p b *
        ((finrank k (Y ⟶ Q b (κ b + 1)) : ℤ) - finrank k (kernel f ⟶ Q b (κ b + 1))) :=
      Finset.sum_le_sum fun b _ => key b
    _ = (potential k Q κ p Y : ℤ) - potential k Q κ p (kernel f) := by
      simp only [potential, Nat.cast_sum, Nat.cast_mul, hp', mul_sub, Finset.sum_sub_distrib]

/-- With an integer certificate at `i`, `(Ap)ᵢ ≥ 1`, the potential drops strictly from `Y` to the
kernel of a nonzero `f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)`. -/
theorem potential_kernel_lt [Fintype ι] (H : CartanDescentHypotheses k Q κ A) {p : ι → ℤ}
    (hp : ∀ b, 0 ≤ p b) {i : ι} (hi : 1 ≤ (A *ᵥ p) i) {Y : C} (f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)) (hf : f ≠ 0) :
    potential k Q κ p (kernel f) < potential k Q κ p Y := by
  have := H.mulVec_le_potential_sub hp f hf
  omega

/-! ### The torsion pair -/

/-- **The test class.** An object with no nonzero morphism to any `Q i (κ i)` has no nonzero
morphism to `F`: it has none to the `Q i j`, `j ≤ κ i`, which embed in `Q i (κ i)`, and the
objects receiving no nonzero morphism from it are closed under extensions. -/
theorem leftOrthogonal_of_forall_eq_zero (H : CartanDescentHypotheses k Q κ A) {Y : C}
    (hY : ∀ (i : ι) (f : Y ⟶ Q i (κ i)), f = 0) : (torsionFreeClass Q κ).leftOrthogonal Y := by
  have hgen : (generators Q κ).leftOrthogonal Y := by
    rintro _ f ⟨i, j, hj, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := H.exists_mono i j hj
    rw [← cancel_mono m, zero_comp]
    exact hY i (f ≫ m)
  intro X f hX
  exact (generators Q κ).abelianExtensionClosure_le
    (generators Q κ).le_rightOrthogonal_leftOrthogonal X hX f hgen

/-- **Cartan descent.** Given an integer certificate, a vector `p ≥ 0` with `Ap ≥ 1`
componentwise, the objects with no nonzero morphism to `F` and the extension closure `F` of the
objects `Q i j`, `j ≤ κ i`, form a torsion pair `(⊥F, F)`. The potential `L` drops on the
kernels of nonzero morphisms to the `Q i (κ i)` (`mulVec_le_potential_sub`), which replaces a
chain condition (`ObjectProperty.torsionTheory_of_potential`). -/
theorem torsionTheory [Fintype ι] (H : CartanDescentHypotheses k Q κ A) {p : ι → ℤ}
    (hp : ∀ b, 0 ≤ p b) (hAp : ∀ i, 1 ≤ (A *ᵥ p) i) :
    TorsionTheory (torsionFreeClass Q κ).leftOrthogonal (torsionFreeClass Q κ) := by
  refine ObjectProperty.torsionTheory_of_potential _ (fun q => ∃ i, Q i (κ i) = q)
    (potential k Q κ p) (fun Y hY => H.leftOrthogonal_of_forall_eq_zero fun i f => hY ⟨i, rfl⟩ f)
    ?_
  rintro Y _ f ⟨i, rfl⟩ hf
  obtain ⟨j, hj, ⟨e⟩⟩ := H.exists_image_iso i f hf
  exact ⟨(torsionFreeClass Q κ).prop_of_iso e.symm
    ((generators Q κ).le_abelianExtensionClosure _ ⟨i, j, hj, rfl⟩),
    H.potential_kernel_lt hp (hAp i) f hf⟩

/-- **Cartan descent for a positive definite matrix.** If `A` is a positive definite symmetric
Z-matrix, it has an integer certificate (`Matrix.IsZMatrix.posDef_iff_int_certificate`), so
`(⊥F, F)` is a torsion pair. -/
theorem torsionTheory_of_posDef [Fintype ι] (H : CartanDescentHypotheses k Q κ A)
    (hZ : A.IsZMatrix) (hA : A.IsSymm) (hPD : A.PosDef) :
    TorsionTheory (torsionFreeClass Q κ).leftOrthogonal (torsionFreeClass Q κ) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hAp⟩ := (hZ.posDef_iff_int_certificate hA).1 hPD
  exact H.torsionTheory (fun b => (hp b).le) hAp

/-- **Cartan descent for an exceptional fibre.** If `A` is the Cartan matrix of a connected
exceptional fibre (`Mukai.FundamentalCycle`), for a symmetric form, then `(⊥F, F)` is a torsion
pair: the Cartan matrix is a positive definite symmetric Z-matrix
(`Mukai.FundamentalCycle.cartan_posDef`). -/
theorem torsionTheory_of_fundamentalCycle [Fintype ι] {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N]
    {β : N →ₗ[ℤ] N →ₗ[ℤ] ℤ} (Θ : Mukai.FundamentalCycle β ι) (hβ : ∀ x y, β x y = β y x)
    (H : CartanDescentHypotheses k Q κ Θ.cartan) :
    TorsionTheory (torsionFreeClass Q κ).leftOrthogonal (torsionFreeClass Q κ) :=
  H.torsionTheory_of_posDef Θ.cartan_isZMatrix (Θ.cartan_isSymm hβ) (Θ.cartan_posDef hβ)

end CartanDescentHypotheses

end Abelian

end CategoryTheory
